# Line-ending policy for files whose meaning depends on it.
#
# The port carries no prebuilt binaries any more: upstream 0.13 stopped shipping
# per-platform bootstrap binaries, and `bootstrap/launch.mjs` fetches the runtime
# instead. What remains sensitive is the shell wrapper, which `sh` reads literally:
# a CRLF arrival turns a command name into one ending in a carriage return.
install.sh text eol=lf

# The Node launcher is ordinary source, but pinning LF keeps every checkout of it
# byte-identical, which is what a release checksum is computed over.
dsh-unica-plugin/bootstrap/launch.mjs text eol=lf

# Note what this file cannot do: it does NOT carry the executable bit. Git records
# modes from the filesystem, and on Windows git writes 100644 for every file while
# nothing local notices. The `posix-modes` CI job asserts the bit for `install.sh`;
# that job is the guard against a Windows commit dropping it, not this file.
